// Regression case for the build_pattern divergence (NOT fixed by fc46e9db): an
// unknown escape inside a `like` pattern must be a parse error. Cedar rejects
// `like "a\qb"` with `the input \q is not a valid escape`. (Only `\*` -- a
// literal star -- and the standard string escapes are valid in a pattern; `\q`
// is not.)
//
// The current build_pattern is worse than merely accepting it: its
// `Some(other) => Char(other)` arm DROPS the backslash, so `\q` becomes the
// single character `q` and the pattern silently loses a character. Accepted,
// validated, AND mis-decoded.
permit (
    principal,
    action == Drupe::Action::"Read",
    resource
)
when { context.input.document like "a\qb" };
